ee5161c72fb36e57345bbdea02131601cbd3ec5ab67cca6949a5bd"},{"role":"dependence","target":"120dd644125e7d19fdd2fe924df330a9109b1f9f9a9f59f0cc76618416db3e4f"}],"typicality":0.55},{"content":"The isolated artifact 120dd644125e INTEGRATES SRC_003's aggregation mechanism with SRC_002's anchoring critique via a conditional synthesis: the checklist produces genuine accuracy gains through error cancellation when it encodes the correct cue-set (SRC_003), but produces only illusory agreement when it encodes a wrong model (SRC_002); the integrative claim is that both are correct within their respective regimes and the boundary is the checklist's bias relative to expert variance. The integration is REFUTED IF there exists no empirical procedure that can locate which regime a given evaluation is in without oracle access to ground truth, making the integration theoretically coherent but practically unfalsifiable; or if the two mechanisms are not separable — i.e., if error cancellation and shared anchoring operate simultaneously and non-additively, so the boundary condition cannot be cleanly stated as a bias threshold.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"120dd644125e7d19fdd2fe924df330a9109b1f9f9a9f59f0cc76618416db3e4f"},{"role":"dependence","target":"42336906a5e92d5ff05cfcbbd91b4c5f28139baba2860452910e071fa3a1280e"},{"role":"dependence","target":"f8db049e3feda133b7383bd5fb9f13b778ef2aa3e626b04bddb6bb846c5dc31b"}],"typicality":0.4}],"simulation_proposals":[]}